{"content_hash": "35b1eb9e4acb6522", "version_id": 415, "article_id": 42, "level_code": "en_c1", "lang": "en", "level": 5, "level_label": "C1 高级", "title": "Margaret Hamilton, who wrote the code that landed Apollo 11, dies at 90", "title_zh": "写代码送人类登月的玛格丽特·汉密尔顿去世，享年90岁", "has_translation": true, "topic": "science", "source": "guardian_science", "source_url": "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2026/oct/07/margaret-hamilton-moon-computer-software", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1520908695049-da13395b27a6?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8MXx8bWFyZ2FyZXQlMjBoYW1pbHRvbnxlbnwwfDB8fHwxNzkxNTk0Mzc2fDA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Keith Luke on Unsplash", "author": "Keith Luke", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@lukephotography?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/red-house-beside-body-of-water-with-white-motor-boats-during-daytime-Ad2BXIYc_gc?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(116, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(154, 46%, 48%)", "label": "SCIENCE", "seed": "1c94d1b8ff91"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-08", "word_count": 263, "reading_minutes": 1.3, "lead": "Margaret Hamilton, the MIT computer scientist whose software guided Apollo 11 to the lunar surface, has died at 90. Her pioneering work earned her the Presidential Medal of Freedom.", "lead_zh": "麻省理工学院计算机科学家玛格丽特·汉密尔顿去世，享年90岁。她编写的软件引导阿波罗11号登月，开创性贡献为她赢得了总统自由勋章。", "preview": "Margaret Hamilton, the computer pioneer whose software powered the first moon landing, has died, MIT announced on Wednesday. She was 90. In ", "preview_zh": "麻省理工学院周三宣布，计算机先驱玛格丽特·汉密尔顿去世，享年90岁。她的软件为人类首次登月提供了动力。在“软件工程师”和“计算机科学家”等头衔尚未普及的时代，汉密尔顿师从麻省理工学院一位著名气象学家学习编程，随后在该校实验室磨练技艺，编写探测敌机的软件。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 405, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/42/en_c1.mp3", "duration": 105.788, "size_bytes": 638496, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 307, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@fc48a26/content/data/versions/415.json", "paragraphs": ["Margaret Hamilton, the computer pioneer whose software powered the first moon landing, has died, MIT announced on Wednesday. She was 90. In an era before titles like software engineer and computer scientist became mainstream, Hamilton learned to program under a renowned MIT meteorologist, then honed her craft in an MIT laboratory writing software to detect enemy aircraft.", "When MIT won a Nasa contract to develop the Apollo onboard flight software, she seized the chance. \"I was attracted both by the sheer idea and the fact that it had never been done before. I was the first programmer to join and the first woman they hired,\" she told the Guardian in 2019.", "In 1969, minutes before Apollo 11 was to make history by landing on the lunar surface, an onboard computer alarm rang, signalling an emergency. Facing a decision whether to abort, the spacecraft continued. The software was working exactly as Hamilton and her team had intended. \"It quickly became clear the software was not only informing everyone that there was a hardware-related problem but was compensating for it,\" she recalled.", "Barack Obama referenced the incident when he presented her with the Presidential Medal of Freedom in 2016. \"Our astronauts didn't have much time, but thankfully they had Margaret Hamilton,\" he said. She is survived by her daughter, a son-in-law, two grandsons and four great-grandchildren, according to MIT.", "Reflecting on the mission in a 2009 interview with MIT News, Hamilton said: \"Looking back, we were the luckiest people in the world; there was no choice but to be pioneers; no time to be beginners.\""], "paragraphs_zh": ["麻省理工学院周三宣布，计算机先驱玛格丽特·汉密尔顿去世，享年90岁。她的软件为人类首次登月提供了动力。在“软件工程师”和“计算机科学家”等头衔尚未普及的时代，汉密尔顿师从麻省理工学院一位著名气象学家学习编程，随后在该校实验室磨练技艺，编写探测敌机的软件。", "当麻省理工学院获得美国宇航局开发阿波罗机载飞行软件的合同时，她抓住了这个机会。她在2019年对《卫报》说：“吸引我的既是这个纯粹的想法，也是它从未被做过的事实。我是第一个加入的程序员，也是他们雇用的第一位女性。”", "1969年，在阿波罗11号即将创造历史、登陆月球表面的几分钟前，机载计算机发出警报，显示紧急情况。面对是否中止任务的抉择，飞船继续前行。软件完全按照汉密尔顿和团队的意图运行。她回忆说：“很快大家就明白，软件不仅告知所有人存在硬件问题，还在补偿它。”", "2016年，巴拉克·奥巴马在授予她总统自由勋章时提到了这一事件。他说：“我们的宇航员时间不多，但幸运的是他们有玛格丽特·汉密尔顿。”据麻省理工学院称，她的女儿、女婿、两个孙子和四个曾孙健在。", "在2009年接受麻省理工学院新闻采访时，汉密尔顿回顾这次任务说：“回首往事，我们是世界上最幸运的人；除了做先驱别无选择；没有时间做初学者。”"], "body": "Margaret Hamilton, the computer pioneer whose software powered the first moon landing, has died, MIT announced on Wednesday. She was 90. In an era before titles like software engineer and computer scientist became mainstream, Hamilton learned to program under a renowned MIT meteorologist, then honed her craft in an MIT laboratory writing software to detect enemy aircraft.\n\nWhen MIT won a Nasa contract to develop the Apollo onboard flight software, she seized the chance. \"I was attracted both by the sheer idea and the fact that it had never been done before. I was the first programmer to join and the first woman they hired,\" she told the Guardian in 2019.\n\nIn 1969, minutes before Apollo 11 was to make history by landing on the lunar surface, an onboard computer alarm rang, signalling an emergency. Facing a decision whether to abort, the spacecraft continued. The software was working exactly as Hamilton and her team had intended. \"It quickly became clear the software was not only informing everyone that there was a hardware-related problem but was compensating for it,\" she recalled.\n\nBarack Obama referenced the incident when he presented her with the Presidential Medal of Freedom in 2016. \"Our astronauts didn't have much time, but thankfully they had Margaret Hamilton,\" he said. She is survived by her daughter, a son-in-law, two grandsons and four great-grandchildren, according to MIT.\n\nReflecting on the mission in a 2009 interview with MIT News, Hamilton said: \"Looking back, we were the luckiest people in the world; there was no choice but to be pioneers; no time to be beginners.\"", "body_zh": "麻省理工学院周三宣布，计算机先驱玛格丽特·汉密尔顿去世，享年90岁。她的软件为人类首次登月提供了动力。在“软件工程师”和“计算机科学家”等头衔尚未普及的时代，汉密尔顿师从麻省理工学院一位著名气象学家学习编程，随后在该校实验室磨练技艺，编写探测敌机的软件。\n\n当麻省理工学院获得美国宇航局开发阿波罗机载飞行软件的合同时，她抓住了这个机会。她在2019年对《卫报》说：“吸引我的既是这个纯粹的想法，也是它从未被做过的事实。我是第一个加入的程序员，也是他们雇用的第一位女性。”\n\n1969年，在阿波罗11号即将创造历史、登陆月球表面的几分钟前，机载计算机发出警报，显示紧急情况。面对是否中止任务的抉择，飞船继续前行。软件完全按照汉密尔顿和团队的意图运行。她回忆说：“很快大家就明白，软件不仅告知所有人存在硬件问题，还在补偿它。”\n\n2016年，巴拉克·奥巴马在授予她总统自由勋章时提到了这一事件。他说：“我们的宇航员时间不多，但幸运的是他们有玛格丽特·汉密尔顿。”据麻省理工学院称，她的女儿、女婿、两个孙子和四个曾孙健在。\n\n在2009年接受麻省理工学院新闻采访时，汉密尔顿回顾这次任务说：“回首往事，我们是世界上最幸运的人；除了做先驱别无选择；没有时间做初学者。”", "text": "Margaret Hamilton, the computer pioneer whose software powered the first moon landing, has died, MIT announced on Wednesday. She was 90. In an era before titles like software engineer and computer scientist became mainstream, Hamilton learned to program under a renowned MIT meteorologist, then honed her craft in an MIT laboratory writing software to detect enemy aircraft. When MIT won a Nasa contract to develop the Apollo onboard flight software, she seized the chance. \"I was attracted both by the sheer idea and the fact that it had never been done before. I was the first programmer to join and the first woman they hired,\" she told the Guardian in 2019. In 1969, minutes before Apollo 11 was to make history by landing on the lunar surface, an onboard computer alarm rang, signalling an emergency. Facing a decision whether to abort, the spacecraft continued. The software was working exactly as Hamilton and her team had intended. \"It quickly became clear the software was not only informing everyone that there was a hardware-related problem but was compensating for it,\" she recalled. Barack Obama referenced the incident when he presented her with the Presidential Medal of Freedom in 2016. \"Our astronauts didn't have much time, but thankfully they had Margaret Hamilton,\" he said. She is survived by her daughter, a son-in-law, two grandsons and four great-grandchildren, according to MIT. Reflecting on the mission in a 2009 interview with MIT News, Hamilton said: \"Looking back, we were the luckiest people in the world; there was no choice but to be pioneers; no time to be beginners.\"", "vocab": [{"word": "trailblazer", "pos": "noun", "zh": "先驱，开拓者", "note": "指在某一领域率先开辟道路的人"}, {"word": "pioneer", "pos": "noun", "zh": "先锋，先驱", "note": "可作名词或动词，强调开创性"}, {"word": "honed", "pos": "verb", "zh": "磨练，锤炼", "note": "常与 skills/craft 搭配"}, {"word": "seized the chance", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "抓住机会", "note": "比 take the chance 更强调主动把握"}, {"word": "onboard", "pos": "adj", "zh": "机载的，船载的", "note": "常指交通工具上的设备或系统"}, {"word": "abort", "pos": "verb", "zh": "中止，放弃", "note": "常用于任务、计划或怀孕"}, {"word": "compensating", "pos": "verb", "zh": "补偿，弥补", "note": "这里指软件自动弥补硬件故障"}, {"word": "mechanisms", "pos": "noun", "zh": "机制，方法", "note": "常指系统内的运作方式"}, {"word": "referenced", "pos": "verb", "zh": "提及，引用", "note": "比 mention 更正式"}, {"word": "survived by", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "由……健在（指遗属）", "note": "讣告常用语，后接亲属"}, {"word": "Reflecting on", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "回顾，反思", "note": "用于引出对往事的思考"}, {"word": "sheer", "pos": "adj", "zh": "纯粹的，十足的", "note": "强调程度，如 sheer luck"}, {"word": "mainstream", "pos": "adj", "zh": "主流的", "note": "指被广泛接受或常见的"}, {"word": "renowned", "pos": "adj", "zh": "著名的，闻名的", "note": "比 famous 更正式"}], "title_original": "Margaret Hamilton, trailblazer whose software powered Apollo 11 moon landing, dies aged 90", "summary_original": "MIT computer scientist led development of software for moon mission and earned Presidential Medal of Freedom\nMargaret Hamilton, the computer pioneer whose software powered the first moon landing, has died, the Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT)\nannounced\non Wednesday. She was 90.\nIn an era before titles such as software engineer and computer scientist became mainstream, Hamilton, who died on 30 September, learned to program under the tutelage of a renowned MIT meteorologist.\nContinue reading...", "body_original": "Margaret Hamilton, trailblazer whose software powered Apollo 11 moon landing, dies aged 90\nMIT computer scientist led development of software for moon mission and earned Presidential Medal of Freedom\nMargaret Hamilton, the computer pioneer whose software powered the first moon landing, has died, the Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT)\nannounced\non Wednesday. She was 90.\nIn an era before titles such as software engineer and computer scientist became mainstream, Hamilton, who died on 30 September, learned to program under the tutelage of a renowned MIT meteorologist.\nShe continued to perfect the craft in an MIT laboratory, writing software that could detect enemy aircraft. When the institute received a Nasa contract to develop the Apollo onboard flight software, she jumped at the opportunity.\n“I was attracted both by the sheer idea and the fact that it had never been done before. I was the first programmer to join and the first woman they hired,” she\ntold\nthe Guardian in 2019.\nIn 1969, minutes before the\nApollo 11\nspacecraft was set to make history by landing on the lunar surface, an onboard computer’s alarm rang, indicating an emergency.\nFaced with a decision of whether to abort the mission, the spacecraft continued on. The software was working just as Hamilton and her team intended.\n“It quickly became clear the software was not only informing everyone that there was a hardware-related problem but was compensating for it – restarting and re-establishing the highest priority tasks. The error detection and recovery mechanisms had come to the rescue,” Hamilton said.\nBarack Obama referenced the incident when he presented her with the Presidential Medal of Freedom in 2016.\n“Our astronauts didn’t have much time, but thankfully they had Margaret Hamilton,” he said.\nHamilton is survived by her daughter, a son-in-law, two grandsons and four great-grandchildren,\naccording\nto MIT.\nReflecting on the mission, in a 2009\ninterview\nwith MIT News, Hamilton said: “Looking back, we were the luckiest people in the world; there was no choice but to be pioneers; no time to be beginners.”\nExplore more on these topics\nSpace\nApollo 11\nThe moon\nComputing\nnews\nShare\nReuse this content", "fetched_at": "2026-10-10T01:06:14.236394", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "Margaret", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.537, "sm": 100, "em": 537, "cs": 0, "ce": 8, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "Hamilton", "s": 0.55, "e": 1.113, "sm": 550, "em": 1112, "cs": 9, "ce": 17, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": ",", "s": 1.113, "e": 1.413, "sm": 1112, "em": 1412, "cs": 17, "ce": 18, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "the", "s": 1.413, "e": 1.525, "sm": 1412, "em": 1525, "cs": 19, "ce": 22, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "computer", "s": 1.538, "e": 2.013, "sm": 1537, "em": 2012, "cs": 23, "ce": 31, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "pioneer", "s": 2.025, "e": 2.562, "sm": 2025, "em": 2562, "cs": 32, "ce": 39, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "whose", "s": 2.575, "e": 2.75, "sm": 2575, "em": 2750, "cs": 40, "ce": 45, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "software", "s": 2.763, "e": 3.288, "sm": 2762, "em": 3287, "cs": 46, "ce": 54, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "powered", "s": 3.3, "e": 3.662, "sm": 3300, "em": 3662, "cs": 55, "ce": 62, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": "the", "s": 3.675, "e": 3.75, "sm": 3675, "em": 3750, "cs": 63, "ce": 66, "si": 0}, {"i": 10, "w": "first", "s": 3.763, "e": 4.088, "sm": 3762, "em": 4087, "cs": 67, "ce": 72, "si": 0}, {"i": 11, "w": "moon", "s": 4.1, "e": 4.337, "sm": 4100, "em": 4337, "cs": 73, "ce": 77, "si": 0}, {"i": 12, "w": "landing", "s": 4.35, "e": 4.775, "sm": 4350, "em": 4774, "cs": 78, "ce": 85, "si": 0}, {"i": 13, "w": ",", "s": 4.775, "e": 5.112, "sm": 4774, "em": 5112, "cs": 85, "ce": 86, "si": 0}, {"i": 14, "w": "has", "s": 5.112, "e": 5.3, "sm": 5112, "em": 5300, "cs": 87, "ce": 90, "si": 0}, {"i": 15, "w": "died", "s": 5.312, "e": 5.688, "sm": 5312, "em": 5687, "cs": 91, "ce": 95, "si": 0}, {"i": 16, "w": ",", "s": 5.688, "e": 5.862, "sm": 5687, "em": 58